                <pb facs="0448" n="338" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg338"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex 3]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Agreement Relating to the Chientao Region Concluded
                        Between Japan and China, September 4, 1909</hi> (MacMurray—Page 797)</head>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 6.—The Government of China shall undertake
                    to extend the Kirin-Changchun Railway to the southern boundary of Yenchi, and to
                    connect it at Hoiryong (Huining) with a Korean railway, and such extension shall
                    be effected upon the same terms as the Kirin-Changchun Railway. The date of
                    commencing the work of the proposed extension shall be determined by the
                    Government of China, considering the actual requirements of the situation, and
                    upon consultation with the Government of Japan.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
